(C) When a court makes a determination in a contested adoption concerning the best interest of a child, the court shall not consider the age of the petitioner, if the petitioner is authorized to adopt under section 3107.03 of the Revised Code.

(D) The petitioner has the burden of proving the best interest of the child by a preponderance of the evidence.

